#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# accumulate

#% text
# `accumulate(xs)` gives the running sums `[x1, x1 + x2, x1 + x2 + x3, ...]` of the list `xs`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The result has the same length as `xs`; its last element is the total.

#% item
# Elements may be numbers of any kind, symbols or lists of equal length (summed element by element).

#% item
# `accumulate` is defined in the prelude through `fold_list`; for running values of another operation use `fold_list` directly.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
accumulate([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])
#% output
#= [1, 3, 6, 10, 15]

#% cell
accumulate([a, b, c])
#% output
#= [a, a + b, a + b + c]

#% cell
accumulate([])
#% output
#= []

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Fractions and machine reals:

#% cell
accumulate([1/2, 1/4, 1/8, 1/16])
#% output
#= [1/2, 3/4, 7/8, 15/16]

#% cell
accumulate([0.1, 0.1, 0.1])
#% output
#= [0.1, 0.2, 0.30000000000000004]

#% text
# Vectors are summed element by element:

#% cell
accumulate([[1, 0], [0, 1], [1, 1]])
#% output
#= [[1, 0], [1, 1], [2, 2]]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# A random walk from its steps:

#% cell
seed(2); accumulate(random_choice([-1, 1], 12))
#% output
#= [-1, -2, -3, -2, -1, -2, -3, -4, -3, -2, -3, -2]

#% text
# A cumulative distribution from a histogram's counts:

#% cell
counts = [2, 5, 9, 3, 1]
accumulate(counts)/total(counts)
#% output
#= [1/10, 7/20, 4/5, 19/20, 1]

#% text
# The triangular numbers:

#% cell
accumulate(range(10))
#% output
#= [1, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21, 28, 36, 45, 55]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The last running sum is the total:

#% cell
last(accumulate(range(100))) == total(range(100))
#% output
#= true

#% text
# `fold_list` with the start value kept gives one more element:

#% cell
fold_list((a, b) => a + b, 0, [1, 2, 3])
#% output
#= [0, 1, 3, 6]

#% text
# Differences of consecutive running sums give the list back:

#% cell
s = accumulate([3, 1, 4, 1, 5])
prepend(rest(s) - most(s), first(s))
#% output
#= [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `fold_list`, `total`, `sum`, `fold`
